      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is perfectly valid to feel overwhelmed by these existential questions, and questioning the nature of purpose isn't an act of fabrication. Many thinkers across cultures have grappled with the concept of an indifferent universe, and there is a rich diversity of views on whether to seek meaning or embrace the void. What ultimately matters for you is what you find personally satisfying or necessary from your existence. Finding comfort in routines or rules doesn't necessarily mean you've given up on randomness, but rather that you are finding some structure in your life to create meaning in the face of uncertainty.",
